// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`the scenario exports keep pace with the scenario model > renders the whole construct set the same way run to run 1`] = `
"# Onboarding

Create a pet, then read it back.

6 steps, run in order.

## Prerequisites

These variables are referenced by the steps and produced by none of them — set them before running the scenario:

- \`{{auth.apiKey}}\`

## Inputs

Values the scenario carries for its own variables:

- \`{{ownerName}}\` = \`Ada\`

## Step 1 — Create a pet

\`\`\`http
POST /pets
\`\`\`

First we create the pet.

- Timeout: 2500 ms

Sends:

- Header \`X-Key\`: \`{{auth.apiKey}}\`

Body (\`application/json\`):

\`\`\`json
{"name":"Rex","owner":"{{ownerName}}"}
\`\`\`

Asserts:

- Status is \`201\`
- \`/name\` in the response body equals \`Rex\`

Extracts, under the names the later steps reference as \`{{var}}\`:

- \`petId\` — response body at \`/id\`
- \`auth.session\` — response header \`X-Session\` (saved to the environment, sensitive, masked wherever it is shown)

## Step 2 — Read a pet

\`\`\`http
GET /pets/{petId}
\`\`\`

- The scenario carries on even if this step fails.

Sends:

- Path \`petId\`: \`{{petId}}\`
- Query \`verbose\`: \`true\`
- Cookie \`session\`: \`{{auth.session}}\`

Asserts:

- Status in the \`2xx\` range (the default verdict)
- \`/id\` exists in the response body
- \`/status\` in the response body matches \`^avail\`

## Step 3 — Search pets

\`\`\`http
GET /pets
\`\`\`

Sends:

- Query string: \`sort=name&limit=10\`

Asserts:

- Status in the \`2xx\` range (the default verdict)
- JSONPath \`$[?count(@.pets) > 0]\` selects at least one node in the response body

Extracts, under the names the later steps reference as \`{{var}}\`:

- \`firstPet\` — response body, JSONPath \`$.pets[0].id\`

## Step 4 — Create a pet

\`\`\`http
POST /pets
\`\`\`

Sends:

Body (\`application/xml\`):

\`\`\`
<pet><name>Rex</name></pet>
\`\`\`

Asserts:

- Status in the \`2xx\` range (the default verdict)

## Step 5 — Upload a photo

\`\`\`http
POST /pets/{petId}/photo
\`\`\`

Sends:

- Form field \`caption\`: \`Rex at the park\`
- Form field \`photo\`: the file \`rex.png\`, chosen at run time

Asserts:

- Status in the \`2xx\` range (the default verdict)

## Step 6 — Create a pet

\`\`\`http
POST /pets
\`\`\`

Sends:

- Body: the file \`pets.json\`, chosen at run time

Asserts:

- Status in the \`2xx\` range (the default verdict)
"
`;
